│     The fix: `get_parameterless_sub_dependant` in `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` never recorded a security requirement for a parameterless `SecurityBase` dependency (such as `Depends(HTTPBearer())` at app or router level), so its scheme was dropped from the OpenAPI output. It now attaches the `SecurityRequirement`, mirroring what `get_dependant` already does.                     │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                │
│     I confirmed the fix with a reproduction app (app-level `HTTPBearer` plus a router-level `APIKeyHeader`): both schemes now appear in `components.securitySchemes` and in the operations' `security` lists. Two related security test files pass (6 tests). I did not run the wider suite, and I did not add a regression test.                                                              │
